# Second Look creek records, for the VS Code REST Client or IntelliJ HTTP client.
# Same five steps as second-look.postman_collection.json. Point baseUrl at a local HAPI
# (docker run -d --name sl-hapi -p 8085:8080 hapiproject/hapi:latest) or the OneAquaHealth
# sandbox. Delete only ids you created and recorded in fhir/sandbox_ledger.jsonl.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8085/fhir
@tagSystem = https://github.com/alejandro-publius/second-look
@tagCode = second-look
@observationIdentifierSystem = https://github.com/alejandro-publius/second-look/fhir/observation
@locationIdentifierSystem = https://github.com/alejandro-publius/second-look/fhir/location-id
@userAgent = second-look (+https://github.com/alejandro-publius/second-look)

### 1. Create the visit: a transaction of conditional creates, safe to run twice
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: application/fhir+json
Accept: application/fhir+json
User-Agent: {{userAgent}}

< ../golden/visit-strawberry-creek-1.transaction.json

### 2. Read our Observations by tag
GET {{baseUrl}}/Observation?_tag={{tagSystem}}|{{tagCode}}&_count=20
Accept: application/fhir+json
User-Agent: {{userAgent}}

### 3. Read the Provenance by target (from an answer to the person who gave it)
GET {{baseUrl}}/Provenance?target:Observation.identifier={{observationIdentifierSystem}}|visit-0001-channel_form
Accept: application/fhir+json
User-Agent: {{userAgent}}

### 4. Read the spot Location
GET {{baseUrl}}/Location?identifier={{locationIdentifierSystem}}|spot-1
Accept: application/fhir+json
User-Agent: {{userAgent}}

### 5. Delete one Location by id. Replace the id with one from fhir/sandbox_ledger.jsonl.
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/Location/REPLACE-WITH-AN-ID-FROM-THE-LEDGER
Accept: application/fhir+json
User-Agent: {{userAgent}}
